the rolex 24 Hours of Daytona is it the  most popular car race in America and  it's not the richest but running from  240 p.m. saturday to 240 p.m. sunday it  is definitely the longest and with  plenty of racing wealth behind it it is  definitely the most prestigious  the goal of the race is to see how many  times you can complete the three and a  half mile circuit in 24 hours it's a  grueling commitment for the cars the  teams and the spectators so of course I  had to see the Rolex 24 for myself and  it makes perfect sense that this would  be the site of the debut runner for  Ford's new racing car the four GT you  know the one board has hyped it for a  year and we saw the four hundred  thousand dollar production version of it  in Detroit in January expectations were  high for this year's team it's three  drivers would have to alternate quickly  while on the track if a car looks good  it usually goes fast there's a lot of  performance in the car that we haven't  even tapped yet before the race throngs  of fans mostly American crowded around  the car watching this machine get  prepped for his long haul was pretty  intense and you could feel the energy in  the garage as the driving team practice  the switch offs they'd make over the  course of the race  the GT started strong but was quickly  overtaken by some race veterans from  Porsche Audi and Corvette and the Ford  GT had some shall we say growing pains  throughout the race alternately stalling  spinning and heading into the pits for  mechanical adjustments then again in  this racing series that is to be  expected  in the hours between pit stops the crew  grabbed catnaps where they could but  it's hard to sleep when some of the  fastest cars in the world are jockeying  for position just feet away  in the end the Ford GT didn't quite do  as well as poked Honda one in the  overall standings the Ford GT finished  in the middle of its class ford is going  to win it's a question about when they  might not win the roads 24 but they are  going to win at one stage with that car  but all is not lost not by a long shot  this race is a proving ground for the  future the engines brakes suspension and  transmission are all the best and  fastest system sport has developed a  date and as the car races again and  again and again those systems will  improve eventually they will be polished  enough to put into the car soul to  people like you and me I can't wait
 

